{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0032898","isObsolete":false,"name":"neurotrophin production","definition":{"text":"The appearance of a neurotrophin due to biosynthesis or secretion by cells in a neuron's target field, resulting in an increase in its intracellular or extracellular levels. A neurotrophin is any of a family of growth factors that prevent apoptosis in neurons and promote nerve growth."},"children":[{"id":"GO:0032900","relation":"negatively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:0032899","relation":"regulates"},{"id":"GO:0032901","relation":"positively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:0032902","relation":"is_a"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0032501 (multicellular organismal process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044707 (single-multicellular organism process)"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-06","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0043524 (negative regulation of neuron apoptotic process)"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-06","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The appearance of a neurotrophin due to biosynthesis or secretion by cells in a neuron's target field, resulting in an increase in its intracellular or extracellular levels. A neurotrophin is any of a family of growth factors that prevent apoptosis in neurons and promote nerve growth."},{"timestamp":"2013-07-06","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The appearance of a neurotrophin due to biosynthesis or secretion by cells in a neuron's target field, resulting in an increase in its intracellular or extracellular levels